      "type": "llm_response",
      "reasoning": "Opponent is attacking with Patron of the Valiant (4/4 flying) and Trusty Retriever (4/5). Tempered Veteran has vigilance now but they chose not to attack with it - smart, keeping it untapped for its ability.\n\
\n\
Let me evaluate blocking:\n\
- Patron of the Valiant: 4/4 FLYING - I can't block it with Markov Warlord (no flying). Takes 4 damage.\n\
- Trusty Retriever: 4/5 - I can block with Markov Warlord (4/4). Warlord deals 4, Retriever survives at 4/1. Retriever deals 4, Warlord dies. Bad trade for me since Warlord is my only creature.\n\
\n\
Wait - opponent has 3 untapped Plains + Tempered Veteran with vigilance. Veteran can tap with {W} to put a +1/+1 counter on Retriever (which has +1/+1 counters). So if I block Retriever, they can pump it to 5/6 and my Warlord still dies while Retriever survives at 5/2. \n\
\n\
If I don't block: I take 4+4 = 8 damage, going from 18 to 10. That's rough but I keep my Warlord.\n\
\n\
If I block Retriever: I take 4 from Patron (18→14), but lose my Warlord to Retriever. And they still have everything.\n\
\n\
I should not block. Taking 8 puts me to 10, but I keep Markov Warlord and can cast Scholar next main phase for a massive swing. Scholar + Meteor Golem from graveyard would be huge.",
