      "decision_index": 79,
    },
    {
      "severity": "minor",
      "description": "Shining Armor has flash, so casting it in the precombat main phase wastes its surprise value. It could be held to use as a combat trick during blocks or on the opponent's turn to blank removal. Additionally, Bulwark Giant for 5 life and a 3/6 body might be the stronger play at 15 life against an aggressive red deck with Markov Warlord threatening damage.",
      "action_taken": "Cast Shining Armor in precombat main phase, giving away information before combat.",
      "better_line": "Either hold Shining Armor (flash) and cast Jousting Lance + equip for an aggressive attack, or cast Bulwark Giant to gain 5 life and stabilize. Shining Armor should be kept in hand to use as a surprise during combat or on opponent's turn.",
      "type": "blunder",
